{
  "name": "create-connector-between-compatible-interfaces",
  "description": "A connector whose two ports name two DIFFERENT interfaces, joined because the required one is satisfied by the provided one: every data element of `IStatusNarrow` has a counterpart of the same name and the same resolved type in `IStatusWide`. The standard's condition (`[constr_1069]` 1(a)) rather than name equality.",
  "kind": "example",
  "context": {
    "summary": "The `examples/basic` model, which declares `ExampleSWC`, `ExampleConsumerSWC` and the value types `float32` and `uint8`, and neither of the two interfaces the change set creates. One unit creates both interfaces, a port on each component, and the connector between them.",
    "existing_elements": [
      {
        "layer": "swc",
        "element": "ExampleSWC"
      },
      {
        "layer": "swc",
        "element": "ExampleConsumerSWC"
      },
      {
        "layer": "implementation_types",
        "element": "float32"
      },
      {
        "layer": "implementation_types",
        "element": "uint8"
      }
    ],
    "baseline_state": "current",
    "authorization": {
      "approved_scope": [
        {
          "operation": "create",
          "address": {
            "layer": "interfaces",
            "element": "IStatusWide"
          }
        },
        {
          "operation": "create",
          "address": {
            "layer": "interfaces",
            "element": "IStatusNarrow"
          }
        },
        {
          "operation": "create",
          "address": {
            "layer": "swc",
            "element": "ExampleSWC",
            "path": [
              {
                "field": "ports"
              },
              {
                "member": "pStatus"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "operation": "create",
          "address": {
            "layer": "swc",
            "element": "ExampleConsumerSWC",
            "path": [
              {
                "field": "ports"
              },
              {
                "member": "rStatus"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "operation": "create",
          "address": {
            "layer": "connectors",
            "element": "Status_Wide_to_Narrow"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "notes": "The two interfaces share no name and the element they share is typed by the same declared value type on both sides, so the same-name short-circuit answers nothing here and the verdict is the widened condition's. Nothing is seeded: the exchange states its own two interfaces, which is what lets a connector between two different interfaces be shown against the unmodified base model."
  },
  "input": {
    "operation": "change_set",
    "baseline": "rev1:2f8c41a6d0b7e593",
    "intent": "Join the narrow requirer to the wide provider.",
    "operations": [
